{"n":158,"kind":"photograph","description":"Night photograph, letterboxed in phone-screenshot format, taken from an elevated position looking down on an ornate, floodlit Victorian-style corner building with a mansard roof, tree-lined street, queued traffic with red tail lights, and pedestrians. The building and setting are consistent with the Corinthia Hotel London seen from across Northumberland Avenue/Victoria Embankment Gardens. The original filename 'NSA_Traf_CAM_ROT3.png' implies the image is an NSA traffic-camera capture, which cannot be verified from the image itself.","text":"","people":[],"orgs":[],"objects":["hotel building","street traffic","taxis","streetlights"],"places":["London","Corinthia Hotel (probable)"],"terms":["London night","traffic cam","NSA_Traf_CAM","hotel","surveillance"],"flags":["Building identification as the Corinthia Hotel London is probable, not certain; the filename's NSA traffic-camera claim is unverified."],"confidence":"yellow"}
{"n":168,"kind":"screenshot - 4chan","description":"Screenshot of a 4chan post by Q (tripcode !ITPb.qbhqo, 11/09/17, No.148782302) attaching a file named '_AF1_5A_2.png', shown with its thumbnail and the full image below: a photograph taken through an aircraft window at altitude over ocean, with layered clouds, sunset light, and several small islands visible below. The filename implies it was taken aboard Air Force One during Trump's November 2017 Asia trip; the location is not identifiable from the image.","text":"Q !ITPb.qbhqo (ID: Dx5TPc5d ) 11/09/17(Thu)23:31:45 No.148782302. File: _AF1_5A_2.png (988 KB, 720x1280).","people":[],"orgs":[],"objects":["aircraft window view","clouds","ocean","islands"],"places":[],"terms":["Air Force One","AF1","aerial photo","Asia trip","Q proof"],"flags":["The claim that the photo was taken from Air Force One rests only on the filename and Q context; the aircraft and location cannot be verified from the image."],"confidence":"yellow"}
{"n":178,"kind":"screenshot - news article","description":"Screenshot of image 11 of 12 in a Straits Times photo gallery: silhouetted security personnel on the illuminated stepped deck of the Sands SkyPark atop Marina Bay Sands, Singapore, at night on June 11 2018, with the lit city skyline behind. The caption notes North Korean leader Kim Jong Un was expected to visit the SkyPark ahead of the Trump-Kim summit.","text":"11 of 12. Security personnel at Sands SkyPark on June 11, 2018, where North Korean leader Kim Jong Un is expected to visit. ST PHOTO: LINETTE LAI.","people":["Kim Jong Un (named in caption, not pictured)"],"orgs":["The Straits Times","Marina Bay Sands"],"objects":["observation deck","security personnel","skyline"],"places":["Sands SkyPark","Marina Bay Sands","Singapore"],"terms":["Singapore summit","Kim Jong Un","SkyPark","June 2018"],"flags":["Security personnel are unidentified private individuals; Kim Jong Un appears only in the caption's claim of an expected visit."],"confidence":"green"}
{"n":188,"kind":"screenshot - tweet","description":"Screenshot of a verified Donald J. Trump (@realDonaldTrump) tweet dated 6/11/18, defending the upcoming Singapore summit with North Korea: he says hostages are back and missile launches have stopped, dismissing 'haters & losers' and pundits. Contains the original misspellings 'missle' and 'stoped'.","text":"Donald J. Trump @realDonaldTrump. The fact that I am having a meeting is a major loss for the U.S., say the haters & losers. We have our hostages, testing, research and all missle launches have stoped, and these pundits, who have called me wrong from the beginning, have nothing else they can say! We will be fine! 6/11/18, 6:04 PM.","people":["Donald Trump"],"orgs":[],"objects":["tweet"],"places":[],"terms":["Singapore summit","North Korea","hostages","missile launches","missle stoped typo"],"flags":[],"confidence":"green"}
{"n":198,"kind":"photograph","description":"Photograph, letterboxed in phone-screenshot format, of a Google campus bicycle — the distinctive Google-colored cruiser bike (yellow frame with 'Google' logo, red seat and basket, green fenders, blue and red accents) — standing beside a row of empty red bike racks on a sunny landscaped sidewalk. A truck trailer with a partially visible 1-800 number passes on the road behind. Setting is consistent with the Google campus in Mountain View, California, though no signage confirms the exact location.","text":"Google.","people":[],"orgs":["Google"],"objects":["Google bike","bike racks","truck trailer"],"places":["Google campus (probable)","Mountain View (probable)"],"terms":["Google bike","Googleplex","campus","Silicon Valley"],"flags":["Exact location inferred from the Google campus bike and setting, not shown by signage; truck lettering only partially legible."],"confidence":"yellow"}
